CORE
main.c
compile-and-link assertion-check
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^\*\*\*\* WARNING: no body for function
--
An asm goto in a file-local (static) function, built with goto-cc
--export-file-local-symbols.  The kernel's arch_static_branch (static keys)
has this shape.  The asm-goto lowering creates a temporary for the jump
target; storing it as a named sub of the asm code left it unrenamed when the
enclosing function was mangled, so symex aborted with "failed to find
...::tmp_asm_goto_target".  Carrying the target as an operand lets the rename
pass reach it, so symex succeeds and the assertion is proven.
